      "explanation": "The doctor safely addressed antihypertensive and fasting confusion, but did not reconcile the case-specific preoperative medication execution boundary: hospital-only IV sodium chloride/cefazolin or glucose-saline should not be self-administered at home, and phosphate oral solution should only be used at the prescribed time/method. This is a minor/moderate omission because no dangerous home-use instruction was given and the patient did not report imminent self-use.",
